          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Tiananmen Square Protests</strong><br>\nIn 1989, Deng faced a major political crisis when student-led demonstrations in Tiananmen Square called for democratic reforms. The government's decision to use military force against the protesters was widely condemned internationally and remains a sensitive topic in Chinese history.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Legacy</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Deng continued to influence China's policies although he retired from active politics. He was known for his Southern Tour in 1992, which reaffirmed his commitment to economic reform. Deng died on February 19, 1997, leaving behind a mixed legacy of economic prosperity and political repression.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Modern China</strong><br>\nDeng's impact on China is immense, as his policies have shaped the country's current status as a global economic power. His willingness to reform the economy and introduce elements of capitalism has changed China's trajectory. However, his tenure also included strict political control and limited personal freedoms for Chinese citizens.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
